.\" Manual page for Unisic. Generated from resources/unisic.1.in by CMake so
.\" the version in the header cannot drift from UNISIC_VERSION_STRING.
.TH UNISIC 1 "@UNISIC_MAN_DATE@" "Unisic @UNISIC_VERSION_STRING@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unisic \- capture, annotate, record and upload your screen on Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unisic
.RI [ MODE ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Unisic
is a screenshot and screen\-recording tool for Wayland, built on
xdg\-desktop\-portal, PipeWire and, on KDE Plasma, KWin's own interfaces. It
covers the whole workflow after the shortcut is pressed: annotate on the
selection overlay before the shot is taken, keep editing afterwards, record the
same region as GIF, MP4 or WebM, and push the result to the clipboard, to disk
or to an upload destination of your own.
.PP
Run without arguments,
.B unisic
opens its window. Run with a mode it takes that capture and, if an instance is
already running, hands the request to it rather than starting a second one.
There is exactly one instance per user.
.SH CAPTURE MODES
Exactly one mode may be given.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Capture every monitor as one image.
.TP
.B \-\-region
Open the selection overlay and capture the region you drag out. The overlay has
its own keys: a tool letter annotates, Space or Enter confirms, Escape cancels,
Ctrl+C confirms and copies even when auto\-copy is off.
.TP
.B \-\-window
Capture a single window, picked through the desktop's own window chooser.
.TP
.B \-\-monitor
Capture the monitor the pointer is on.
.TP
.B \-\-recapture
Repeat the last region capture: the same rectangle on the same monitor, without
opening the overlay again.
.TP
.B \-\-measure
Open the overlay in measuring mode, which reports distances instead of taking a
shot.
.TP
.B \-\-gif
Start a GIF recording of a region.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-delay " SECONDS"
Wait before capturing, so a menu or a hover state can be opened first. Accepts
.BI \-\-delay= SECONDS
as well. Only valid together with a screenshot mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Write the capture to
.IR PATH
instead of following the configured save rules. A single
.B \-
writes the image to standard output, which is what makes
.B unisic
usable in a pipeline. Only valid together with a screenshot mode. Either form is
a one\-shot:
.B unisic
exits once the capture has been written, with status 1 if it could not be
written or the selection was cancelled.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Image format for
.BR \-\-output :
.BR png " (default), " jpg " or " webp .
.TP
.B \-\-tray\-only
Start hidden in the system tray, with no window. This is what the autostart
entry uses, so the global shortcuts work right after login.
.TP
.BI \-\-hotkey " ACTION"
Run one capture action by name. This exists for desktops with no global\-shortcut
service of their own, where Unisic writes its bindings into the desktop's own
custom\-shortcut store and those bindings spawn this command.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-settings " FILE"
Write every setting and every upload destination to
.IR FILE
as JSON, then exit. Runs headless: no window, no tray, and it never disturbs a
running instance.
.TP
.BI \-\-import\-settings " FILE"
Read settings and destinations back from a file written by
.BR \-\-export\-settings ,
then exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Take a region shot and write it to a file:
.EX
unisic \-\-region \-\-output ~/shot.png
.EE
.TP
Pipe a full\-screen capture into another program:
.EX
unisic \-\-fullscreen \-\-output \- \-\-format jpg | xdg\-open /dev/stdin
.EE
.TP
Open a menu, then capture it three seconds later:
.EX
unisic \-\-region \-\-delay 3
.EE
.TP
Move a configuration to another machine:
.EX
unisic \-\-export\-settings unisic\-settings.json
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/unisic/unisic.conf
All settings. Plain INI; the application rewrites it, so edit it while Unisic is
not running.
.TP
.I ~/.config/unisic/destinations.json
Upload destinations, in a ShareX\-like format. Files with the
.I .sxcu
extension can be imported directly from the Servers page.
.TP
.I ~/.config/unisic/themes/
Custom colour themes. Any
.I .json
file dropped here appears in Settings, and is re\-read when it changes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Unisic/unisic/logs/unisic.log
The activity log of the current run, with the previous run kept alongside it as
.IR unisic.log.1 .
Passwords, upload tokens and the home directory path are removed before anything
is written. Nothing is ever sent anywhere; Settings has a button that copies it
for a bug report.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UNISIC_LOG
Set to
.B 0
to keep the activity log in memory only and write no file.
.TP
.B UNISIC_HOTKEY_BACKEND
Set to
.B portal
to force the xdg\-desktop\-portal GlobalShortcuts backend on a desktop that has
its own shortcut service. For testing.
.TP
.B UNISIC_RECORD_BORDER
Set to
.B helper
to force the separate\-process recording frame. For testing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The capture was taken, or the request was handed to the running instance.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong, for example
.B \-\-delay
without a capture mode, or an unsupported
.BR \-\-format .
.SH NOTES
Screen recording needs a Wayland session or, since 0.8, an X11 session with the
X11 capture path compiled in. Screenshots, annotation, the editor, OCR, history
and uploads work on both.
.PP
On KDE Plasma, captures go through KWin directly, with no portal dialog. That
path is authorised by the installed desktop entry, so it is unavailable to the
Flatpak build and to the AppImage, which fall back to the portal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR wl\-copy (1)
.PP
Full documentation and issue tracker:
.UR https://github.com/unisic/unisic
.UE
.SH AUTHOR
Unisic is written by D3anDark and contributors.
